  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltbrgtOur project aims to assist people displaced by conflict in Kalay Township, Sagaing (Northwest), Myanmar. Here is a comprehensive overview of how we plan to support them.ltbrgtltbgtShelterlt/bgtltbrgtlt/pgtltulgtltligtWe will provide materials and assistance to improve living conditions, ensuring families have a safe and secure place to stay.lt/ligtlt/ulgtltpgtProtection AwarenessWe will conduct awareness sessions on protecting against exploitation and abuse and understanding gender-based violence. These sessions empower individuals to recognize and respond to risks effectively.ltbrgtltbgtExplosive Ordnance Risk Education (EORE)lt/bgtltbrgtlt/pgtltulgtltligtHazard Education: Given the danger from landmines and explosives in conflict-affected areas, we will educate community members on identifying and avoiding these hazards, promoting safety for all.lt/ligtlt/ulgtltpgtltbgtWASH (Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene)lt/bgtltbrgtlt/pgtltulgtltligtAccess to clean water and proper sanitation is critical for health, especially during the monsoon seasons. We will improve water sources and promote hygiene practices through awareness sessions to prevent disease outbreaks.lt/ligtlt/ulgtltpgtltbgtNutritional Supportlt/bgtltbrgtlt/pgtltulgtltligtWe will provide Cash Voucher Assistance (CVA) (and/or provision of food baskets is an alternative) to increase access to a nutritious diet to enhancement of dietary diversity and access to enriched foods that meet nutritional requirements for vulnerable children and prevent the deterioration in the nutritional status of at-risk groups by providing Cash and Voucher Assistance (CVA) to cover the needs of household and individuals admitted in integrated management of acute malnutrition (IMAM) programme and households and individuals of high-risk group (6-23 months and Pregnant and Lactating Women (PLW)) in Kalay Township.lt/ligtlt/ulgtltpgtltbgtCollaboration and Sustainabilitylt/bgtltbrgtThrough collaboration with local partners and communities, our project addresses immediate needs while building resilience and fostering sustainable recovery. By ensuring aid reaches those most in need and promoting safety and dignity for all, we aim to support the long-term well-being of displaced families in Kalay Townshipltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
